WEBVTT

NOTE tts=synthetic

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.533
Why do breaker retainer keys break?

2
00:00:02.533 --> 00:00:11.700
Run without the tool resting on a surface, the piston blow drives the tool forward and the key takes that load.

3
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:18.733
A worn key slot on the tool or slack bushings let the tool work at an angle and put shock loads on the key.

4
00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:26.667
Without grease the key and the tool slot rub dry and notch; a notched key breaks under impact.

5
00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:34.767
Use the key and its retaining pin made for your breaker model together; do not straighten and refit a bent or cracked key.
